title The headline that outran its own tool
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, deep-read council-rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment.
think Read the running thread first. The last three laps read rota rows 0, 1, and 2, so this lap reads row 3 -- Water and Venus, care and flow: Gall's Law, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. All three shaped what followed rather than decorating it.
think Standfast opened the lap, and this time the ledger was not clean. Running the monotone guard printed rows=126 while the living pin's own headline read Rows: 125 -- a paragraph that names that very witness as its source. Three numbers had drifted together: the total, the span (1 to 125), and the derived remainder (105 where the arithmetic gives 106).
think The drift was exactly one lap old. Row %126 landed and closed in the previous round, the same round that corrected this headline from a prior drift. Booking a row and republishing the total are two acts, and only the first was ever guarded -- so the correction was always going to go stale on the next row.
think REDS %110 had already answered this class once by deriving the number rather than reciting it, and the derivation still has to be typed by a hand on the lap the row lands. Third drift in one paragraph is a lantern that has fired twice over, so the answer is a loom rather than a more careful hand.
think The happy zone named the shape of that loom. The monotone scan already counts the spine; what was missing was a contract check on the publishing side -- one seam, two small answers, the check living with the publisher. So tools/fixtures/reds_ledger_headline_scan.sh reads the headline's three numbers back out of the prose and refuses headline_drift naming exactly which one disagrees.
think Proven on the living tree exactly as it stood: the scan refused all three drifted numbers before a single one was corrected. That is the RED path on real bytes rather than on a control.
obs The guard refused its own author within the minute. Booking row %127 moved the spine from 126 to 127, so the headline corrected moments earlier went stale on the same lap -- and the witness reddened by name rather than passing quietly. Better evidence for the loom than any argument for it.
obs Gall's Law priced the design. The counting scan already worked, so the publishing check grew beside it as a second small thing rather than as a redesigned ledger guard; each half stays readable alone.
obs REDS %126's second half closes here too. That row named a witness sitting in tools/gen/season/ on no roster with nothing to call it, and repaired only the equality -- so the guard would have stayed unrun. It is rung 9/9 of the era suite now, the roster whose promise is to be provable on any host, which a guard reading two files can keep.
obs The witness printed two GREEN lines after the first draft, one of them before a later assert. Collapsed to a single GREEN covering both halves, since a GREEN speaking for part of a subject is REDS %102's own shape.
obs The new rows carried the living pin past its 24,576-byte bound, 19,667 to 25,231. Folded rows 125-126 to crux/archive/ at 19,667 bytes -- the seventeenth such fold, routine, every byte kept and one click away. No cairn: a fold accretes, and the cairn rule governs a debride that cuts.
obs One honest caution rather than a red: a combined recursive grep over crux/ and tools/ returned nothing while a direct grep of the same file found the match. No tree fact was wrong, and the direct check is the one I trusted. A confirming empty result deserves a second look before it becomes a claim.
loom witness=reds_ledger_monotone rows=127 mentions=151 gaps_or_dupes=0 living_pin_bytes=19667 bound=24576
loom suite=glow_tend_era rungs=9 verdict=green
file tools/fixtures/reds_ledger_headline_scan.sh the contract half of the ledger's seam -- the headline recites what the spine measures, or refuses by name
file tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish measures the spine, hands that measurement to the headline scan, asserts agreement, and closes on one GREEN
file tools/glow_tend_era_suite.rish the ledger guard joins the roster as rung 9/9, closing REDS %126's second half
file crux/REDS.md row %127 booked and closed, the headline republished at the measurement, rows 125-126 folded under the pin's bound
file crux/archive/REDS-compiler-and-ledger-guard-rows-125-126.md the folded range, every byte kept
file crux/REMEMBER.md the standing-equipment roster records the new guard and the era suite's ninth rung
recommend keep-going the ledger's own seam is guarded on both sides now, so the next lap is free for the named crux -- the Caravan carry queue after main left it, or the Microkernel Target's agent-doable study rungs
